---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { isPassPlayGameId } from '../games/shared/pass-play';
import { TOOLS } from '../config/tools';

const games = (await getCollection('games')).filter((game) => !game.data.draft);
const passPlayCount = games.filter((game) => isPassPlayGameId(game.id)).length;
const soloCount = games.length - passPlayCount;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About NoCharge"
  description={`About NoCharge: ${games.length} free browser games (${soloCount} solo and ${passPlayCount} Pass & Play), ${TOOLS.length} browser tools, player guides, and no account requirement.`}
  path="/about/"
  showAds={false}
>
  <article class="trust-page prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }]} />
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">About NoCharge</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">A quiet place for free browser games and practical guides.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        NoCharge is a library of {games.length} free browser games: {soloCount} solo games and {passPlayCount} Pass &amp; Play games for two people sharing one device. Alongside the arcade are complete game guides, {TOOLS.length} browser tools, focused articles, reviewed collections, and Quiet Setup editorial. No account is required, and saved game results stay on the device where they were played.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="about-what">
      <h2 id="about-what">What NoCharge is</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/arcade/">Arcade</a> brings together memory and word games, solitaire, number puzzles,
        and turn-taking board games. Solo choices include Memory Match, Minesweeper, Word Search, Mini Sudoku,
        and Sudoku 9×9. Pass &amp; Play includes games such as Reversi, Gomoku, Checkers, and the cooperative
        drawing game Pass the Picture. Each title opens without an account, installation, or profile setup;
        its page explains the rules, supported controls, and which results it saves locally.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site’s Quiet Arcade approach favors clear controls, readable pages, practical game information, and
        respectful optional services over noisy interruptions. The point is to make it easy to play a short round,
        understand a rule, and leave when you are done.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="about-guides">
      <h2 id="about-guides">Games and guide library</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/guides/">guide library</a> documents each live game’s rules, controls, scoring behavior,
        and accessible play options. The <a href="/articles/">article library</a> adds focused examples about a
        single behavior or decision, such as scanning a board or tracing a diagonal letter path. Guides are
        editorial reference material, not a substitute for the game itself or a promise of a result.
      </p>
      <p>
        We update guides and supporting articles when a documented game behavior changes. The{' '}
        <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a> records verified public platform updates.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="about-tools">
      <h2 id="about-tools">Browser tools with worked examples</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/tools/">tool library</a> currently contains {TOOLS.length} utilities and demonstrations.
        Game Finder filters the published catalog; the Session planner estimates runs from session labels.
        The Nonogram clue calculator explains line arrangements, the Sudoku helper lists candidates, and the
        contrast checker compares color luminance. Audio tools include the Ambient Mixer and Singing Bowl Engine.
      </p>
      <p>
        Tool pages explain their inputs, show concrete examples, and state what their results cannot establish.
        A contrast ratio is not a complete accessibility audit, and a suggested session length is not a promise
        about how quickly someone will finish. Calculations use the current browser rather than an uploaded
        player profile.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="about-accounts">
      <h2 id="about-accounts">No-account and local-data model</h2>
      <p>
        NoCharge does not offer user accounts, passwords, cloud saves, or public scoreboards. Game best scores
        and a few preferences are stored in local browser storage on the device you use. They are not uploaded to
        NoCharge or synchronized between devices. You can clear local game data from the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="about-accessibility">
      <h2 id="about-accessibility">Accessibility commitment</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to make the site understandable and usable with keyboard, touch, pointer, and assistive technology
        where the games support them. This includes visible focus, meaningful button names, documented controls,
        pause behavior for timed play, Color Flip’s untimed turn-based mode, and Beacon Lattice’s untimed exact-cover
        board with numeric coverage labels. Accessibility is ongoing work;
        please report a barrier so it can be reviewed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="about-privacy">
      <h2 id="about-privacy">Privacy-first optional services</h2>
      <p>
        Analytics is optional and stays off until a visitor allows it. Advertising is one labeled Google AdSense
        banner at the bottom of eligible pages, with Google&rsquo;s Privacy &amp; messaging consent message managing
        advertising choices and no ads over gameplay. The Privacy page explains those choices, local storage, and
        how to withdraw consent at any time.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="about-operator">
      <h2 id="about-operator">Publisher and contact</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>NoCharge</strong> publishes and operates this game, tool, and guide library at nocharge.net.
        The site's contact address is <a href="mailto:hello@nocharge.net">hello@nocharge.net</a> for support,
        accessibility reports, privacy questions, advertising concerns, and corrections to published rules or examples.
        Please include the relevant page URL and a description of the issue, without passwords or sensitive personal information.
      </p>
      <p>
        Game pages describe NoCharge's implementations rather than claiming every rule matches every physical-game
        variant. Quiet Setup articles carry an evidence label to distinguish editorial research from personal use
        or hands-on testing. A correction can be reported through the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .trust-page {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.15rem;
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .trust-page > header {
    padding: 0.75rem 0 1.25rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .trust-page section {
    padding-top: 0.25rem;
  }

  .trust-page section + section {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
</style>
